msgstr "Belum ada apa-apa — selesaikan cerita seorang gadis untuk menambahkan akhir ceritanya."

msgid "Nothing yet."
msgstr "Belum ada."

msgid "Now start at the alder and sleeves up."
msgstr "Sekarang mulai dari pohon alder, dan gulung lengan bajumu."

msgid "Now that's a circle I'd step out of."
msgstr "Nah, itu baru lingkaran yang mau kutinggalkan."

msgid "Now we can both stop pretending you came over here to talk about books."
msgstr "Sekarang kita berdua bisa berhenti pura-pura kamu datang ke sini untuk membicarakan buku."

msgid "Obviously we're getting the second owl."
msgstr "Tentu saja kita ambil burung hantu kedua."

msgid "Of course I'll help. What does it look like?"
msgstr "Tentu aku akan membantu. Seperti apa bentuknya?"

msgid "Offers appear here once Google Play is reachable."
msgstr "Penawaran muncul di sini setelah Google Play bisa dijangkau."

msgid "Oh, I intend to."
msgstr "Oh, memang itu niatku."

msgid "Oh, that's smooth, why can't anything else this week be smooth?"
msgstr "Oh, mulus sekali. Kenapa tidak ada hal lain minggu ini yang semulus itu?"

msgid "Oh, you're putting it down. Most argue first."
msgstr "Oh, kamu meletakkannya. Kebanyakan berdebat dulu."

msgid "Oh, you're warm... No one's touched me without an axe in years."
msgstr "Oh, kamu hangat... Sudah bertahun-tahun tidak ada yang menyentuhku tanpa kapak."

msgid "Oh. I didn't know I did that. That's embarrassing. Do it again."
msgstr "Oh. Aku tidak tahu aku bisa begitu. Memalukan. Lakukan lagi."

msgid "Ohh... I can feel your heartbeat. In me."
msgstr "Ohh... aku bisa merasakan detak jantungmu. Di dalamku."

msgid "Okay, that one was nice."
msgstr "Oke, yang itu bagus."

msgid "Okay. A small thing."
msgstr "Oke. Sedikit saja."

msgid "Okay. I'm going to say something and you're not allowed to be nice about it."
msgstr "Oke. Aku mau bilang sesuatu dan kamu tidak boleh menanggapinya dengan manis."

msgid "Okay. The stream comes out under the Mill Bridge, in town. Things wash up there. People pick them up."
msgstr "Oke. Sungai itu keluar di bawah Jembatan Kincir, di kota. Barang-barang terdampar di sana. Orang-orang memungutnya."

msgid "Old Glass Marble"
msgstr "Kelereng Kaca Kuno"

msgid "On the way back there's a notice nailed to the Mill Bridge. The town has sold the north woods to an alchemist, for his workshop. Clearing starts on quarter day."
msgstr "Di jalan pulang ada pengumuman dipaku di Jembatan Kincir. Kota sudah menjual hutan utara ke seorang alkemis, untuk bengkelnya. Penebangan dimulai pada hari kuartal."

msgid "Once you've cleared her first chapter, her card on the roster has a gift for her. Give it and her favourite gem shows up more often in all her chapters, for good."
msgstr "Setelah kamu menyelesaikan bab pertamanya, kartunya di lingkaran punya hadiah untuknya. Berikan, dan permata favoritnya akan lebih sering muncul di semua babnya, selamanya."

msgid "One wave and the whole board is dealt again, always with a move to make."
msgstr "Satu kibasan dan seluruh papan diacak ulang, selalu dengan langkah yang bisa dibuat."

msgid "Ooh. That's going in the... sorry."
msgstr "Ooh. Itu masuk ke... maaf."

msgid "Opal"
msgstr "Opal"

msgid "Opal at the baker's counter, a loaf under one arm and a stray button in her hand."
msgstr "Opal di meja toko roti, sebongkah roti di bawah lengan dan sebutir kancing nyasar di tangan."

msgid "Opal moves in properly. Her collection grows a second shelf, then a third: things you've dropped, things your friends have dropped, the ticket from your first evening out together. The jar lives under the bed. She uses it twice that year, both times in thunderstorms, and both times you sit on the floor beside it while she tells you, through the glass, which of the neighbours owe each other money. She climbs out on her own before the storm is over."
msgstr "Opal pindah sungguhan. Koleksinya bertambah satu rak, lalu satu lagi: barang yang kamu jatuhkan, barang yang dijatuhkan teman-temanmu, tiket malam pertama kalian keluar bersama. Stoples itu tinggal di bawah ranjang. Dia memakainya dua kali tahun itu, dua-duanya saat badai petir, dan dua-duanya kamu duduk di lantai di sampingnya sementara dia bercerita, lewat kaca, tetangga mana yang berutang pada siapa. Dia keluar sendiri sebelum badainya reda."

